@*
    The application shell, and nothing more.

    AC4 requires Yello.Client to be running under the AppHost, so the app needs a root
    component to boot at all. It deliberately does not use <Router>: there are no routable
    pages yet, and a Router with an empty route table cannot resolve its NotFound case.
    Routing, the layout and the navigation surface arrive with the screens that need them.

    Superseded 2026-08-27 by story 1.2, which shipped the design foundations. This previously
    read "No markup here carries a class, a style attribute or a colour - story 1.2 owns the
    design foundations", which described story 1.1's tree and became false the moment
    css/tokens.css and css/base.css landed. Recorded as a correction rather than deleted,
    because stale hand-off prose in these files produced six of story 1.1's review findings and
    a seventh at story 1.2's review, which is where this one was caught.

    The shell still carries no class, style attribute or colour of its own, and it does not need
    to: `base.css` styles the document from the tokens, so the shell inherits the body ground,
    the body type role and the focus treatment without naming any of them. The product name
    below is the one literal the externalised-copy gate permits, because a brand is not
    translated.
*@

<p>Yello</p>
